ly videos were not as good in terms  of color and and focus and things like  that is because the webcam was just not  up to it and it's not just the my  computer webcam I had a fancier webcam  that was external but it still wasn't up  to it so eventually I switched to using  a Canon camcorder Vixia camcorder and so  I used that to actually make the videos  and then I just import them separately  and it's a pain in the butt  but I love you folks so much I'm willing  to do it for you so I need to separately  import the video using these little  flash drives to the computer and then  read them into Camtasia and then sync up  the audio and stuff like that but that's  very doable I'm kind of used to doing  equivalent things from doing the podcast  okay I made a mistake and I got a  camcorder that does not have remote  control so I have to walk over it and  push the button and then come back but  that's up that's a minor thing and then  I also have a separate microphone  because I'm a podcaster I have a podcast  mindscape you should all check it out so  I have a fancy podcasting microphone way  more than I need here it is this is an  electro voice our e320 microphone that I  take the audio in I think that the audio  quality probably less important for  youtube videos then for podcasts but  that's okay I can use that it goes right  in there's a little machine that brings  it in from that to the computer but  that's okay Camtasia can bring that in  perfectly well okay and then I put it  all together and that works I think  that's all the software I'm using the  other question is the actual physical  studio setup so studio  here it is one of these directions  oh my left shoulder right shoulder I  don't know because what I'm gonna do is  as I'm editing this video and I'm going  to use Camtasia to import a picture of  the studio set up so it's not a very  complicated studio setup it's my office  I don't have a lot of room but what I  did was I went to Sammy's camera  Sammy's with one M which is a chain that  has stores in throughout California  there's one in Pasadena near Cal Tech so  I had no idea what I was doing I knew  that I want to do these videos with a  green screen and honestly I don't need  the green screen I could just do it in  my office but I need to keep myself  entertained somehow so I thought that'd  be a fun extra thing to learn so I went  in to Sammy's camera and I explained  what I wanted to do and there was a  woman working there who had been a  portrait photographer and she knew  exactly what I was talking about and she  said well you need this and this and  this and you know you see these lights  with the umbrellas and everything and  the green screen is pretty big and I  needed a big setup a pole to hang the  green screen oh and I'm like wow this is  way more than I thought it was gonna be  she explained all why I would need it  and she turned out to be completely  correct so I kind of didn't believe her  but you know as you know the video  quality has improved over the past few  videos because I was learning more and  more about the lighting setup you have  to light the green screen brightly  without lighting yourself too brightly  but you have to light yourself so you  don't look pink or anything like that  and it turned out that what I eventually  learned by trial and error is what she  was trying to tell me all along so I'm  sorry I forgot your name person from  Sammy's camera who helped me out but I  went there literally like three days  before we went into lockdown here in Los  Angeles and the store closed so after we  already knew after restaurants had  already closed but before other stores  had closed I didn't trust myself to buy  things correctly on the internet I  wanted to talk to a real person so I  went there and she told me what to buy  and I just decided to accept her wisdom  there and I bought it and so it's  turning out pretty well  there yeah there's a lot of tricks there  like not only do I have to worry about  what color I'm wearing but  so if I wore green obviously that would  be bad but I've been on you know videos  before I've been on you know Nova and  The History Channel and through the  wormhole with Morgan Freeman and when  you're on green-screen they tell you not  to wear black and I never quite  understood that but now I get it like  somehow it's not that black is the same  as green but that the adjustment there's  a exposure adjustment that happens if  you're too dark it over exposes the  green behind you and becomes harder to  remove or at least that's my current  interpretation of it so anyway that's my  setup then why am I forgetting anything  important here you know a bunch of  little drives and and everything I'm  still struggling with the fact that the  videos are huge file sizes like 60  gigabytes is the Camtasia file when it  finally outputs an mp4 that I can upload  to YouTube it's smaller than that but  the working you know Camtasia format is  really really big and it I don't think  it should be that big and it's a  struggle to put it on my computer with  the disk space but I'm learning about  that anyway probably not many of you  wanted to know that but I'm glad someone  asked this is where I'm gonna put it so  if anyone wants to know they can look  there as I've said before I hope you are  enjoying it I am enjoying making it it's  it takes time but it's useful time it's  good to think about this stuff and it's  good to you know distract yourself a  little bit I like you know I could just  play video games or watch movies all day  this is enormously more rewarding than  that so thank you very much for watching
 

